 * object stores a fresh `_clone` reference for the reader to adopt;
 * decoding adopts each object reference, and T_free destroys it. T_free
 * releases only what T_read or T_decode allocated; never call it on a
 * value that borrows caller memory.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

